<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>A box with a given diagonal</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Kendi wants a closed box whose longest straight rod, from one corner to the opposite corner, is exactly {@dd@} cm. Give whole-number edge lengths for such a box.</p><div>Length [[input:ans1]] cm [[validation:ans1]]</div><div>Width [[input:ans2]] cm [[validation:ans2]]</div><div>Height [[input:ans3]] cm [[validation:ans3]]</div><div>[[feedback:prt1]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>The rod is the space diagonal, so the edges must satisfy \(l^2 + w^2 + h^2 = {@dd@}^2 = {@dsq@}\). For example \({@ta1@}^2 + {@ta2@}^2 + {@ta3@}^2 = {@dsq@}\). All the whole-number boxes, up to order: {@allb@}.</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[dlist: [[3,[1,2,2],[[1,2,2]]],[6,[2,4,4],[[2,4,4]]],[9,[4,4,7],[[1,4,8],[3,6,6],[4,4,7]]],[23,[6,13,18],[[3,6,22],[3,14,18],[6,13,18]]],[12,[4,8,8],[[4,8,8]]],[13,[3,4,12],[[3,4,12]]],[15,[5,10,10],[[2,5,14],[2,10,11],[5,10,10]]],[18,[8,8,14],[[2,8,16],[6,12,12],[8,8,14]]],[19,[6,10,15],[[1,6,18],[6,6,17],[6,10,15]]],[21,[8,11,16],[[4,5,20],[4,8,19],[4,13,16],[6,9,18],[7,14,14],[8,11,16]]]];
/* Design: give a box with a given diagonal; any box with the property scores. One diagnostic node covers both "squares add to d" and "edges add to d", with both feedbacks, because no fixed test triple reaches either one alone on every entry (d = 13, 15 have no positive triple with squares adding to d; d = 3's only triple with edges adding to 3 also has squares adding to 3). Source: original. */
ix: 1+rand(10); DD: dlist[ix];
dd: DD[1]; tb: DD[2]; BX: DD[3]; dsq: dd^2;
ta1: tb[1]; ta2: tb[2]; ta3: tb[3];
alt: if length(BX) > 1 then first(sublist(BX, lambda([b], is(b # tb)))) else [tb[3], tb[1], tb[2]];
bstr(b) := sconcat("(", b[1], ", ", b[2], ", ", b[3], ")");
cands: apply(append, makelist(apply(append, makelist(makelist([a,b,c], c, b, 5), b, a, 5)), a, 1, 5));
sqc: sublist(cands, lambda([t], is(t . t = dd))); sqt: if sqc = [] then [1,1,dd-2] else sqc[1];
s1: sqt[1]; s2: sqt[2]; s3: sqt[3]; al1: alt[1]; al2: alt[2]; al3: alt[3]; tg1: ta1+1; dm2: dd-2;
allb: simplode(map(bstr, BX), "; ");
]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
